<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy Policy · Enhanced Screen Capture</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for the Enhanced Screen Capture browser extension. No data is collected; everything stays on your device." />
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light dark;
        --bg: #f6f7fb;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --border: #e2e5ee;
        --text: #1a1f33;
        --muted: #5f6680;
        --accent: #4f46e5;
        --accent-soft: #eef0ff;
        --code: #f0f2f8;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --bg: #0f1117;
          --surface: #171a23;
          --border: #2a2f3e;
          --text: #e8eaf2;
          --muted: #9aa1b8;
          --accent: #8b84ff;
          --accent-soft: #24223f;
          --code: #222636;
        }
      }
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        font: 16px/1.65 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 760px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 48px 16px 64px;
      }
      .card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: 36px 32px;
      }
      header {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 14px;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .logo {
        flex: none;
        width: 44px;
        height: 44px;
        border-radius: 11px;
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6);
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 26px;
        line-height: 1.25;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .updated {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 14px;
        margin: 0 0 24px;
      }
      h2 {
        margin: 32px 0 8px;
        font-size: 19px;
      }
      p,
      ul {
        margin: 0 0 14px;
      }
      ul {
        padding-left: 22px;
      }
      li {
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .highlight {
        background: var(--accent-soft);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 16px 18px;
        margin: 8px 0 14px;
      }
      code {
        font: 13.5px/1.4 ui-monospace, "Cascadia Code", Consolas, monospace;
        background: var(--code);
        padding: 2px 6px;
        border-radius: 6px;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .table-wrap {
        overflow-x: auto;
        margin: 4px 0 14px;
      }
      table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 15px;
      }
      th,
      td {
        text-align: left;
        vertical-align: top;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      }
      th {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }
      a {
        color: var(--accent);
      }
      footer {
        margin-top: 24px;
        text-align: center;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
      }
      @media (max-width: 560px) {
        main {
          padding-top: 24px;
        }
        .card {
          padding: 24px 18px;
        }
        h1 {
          font-size: 22px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <article class="card">
        <header>
          <div class="logo" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M4 9V5h4M16 4h4v4M20 15v4h-4M8 20H4v-4" />
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.4" fill="#fff" stroke="none" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h1>Privacy Policy: Enhanced Screen Capture</h1>
        </header>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: October 2, 2026</p>

        <p>
          Enhanced Screen Capture is a browser extension for taking screenshots, recording your screen, and annotating
          captures. It is built to work entirely on your device.
        </p>

        <h2>What the extension collects</h2>
        <div class="highlight">
          <strong>Nothing.</strong> The extension does not collect, transmit, sell or share any personal or usage data. It
          has no analytics, telemetry, advertising or tracking code. It makes no network requests.
        </div>

        <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Screenshots and recordings</strong> you take are stored in your browser's local storage (IndexedDB) so
            they appear in the extension's History page. They never leave your device unless you choose to download, copy
            or share them yourself. Only the most recent captures are kept (50 by default, adjustable in Settings), and you
            can delete any or all of them at any time from the History page.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Annotations</strong> you add in the editor are stored locally with the capture.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Settings</strong> (for example your preferred file format) are stored with
            <code>chrome.storage.sync</code>. If you are signed in to Chrome with sync enabled, Chrome syncs these
            preferences between your own devices. They contain no personal data.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Page content</h2>
        <p>
          When you start a capture, the extension temporarily reads the page's layout (scroll size and positions of sticky
          or fixed elements) to stitch a full-page image. It also temporarily adjusts the page's styling so sticky headers
          don't repeat, then restores everything afterwards. Page content is not stored or transmitted, except as the image
          you asked for.
        </p>

        <h2>Microphone, tab audio and screen</h2>
        <p>
          The microphone, tab audio and screen are accessed only while you are recording, and only after you start a
          recording. Chrome shows its own indicators and prompts whenever these are in use. Audio and video go straight
          into the recording file on your device.
        </p>

        <h2>Permissions</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Permission</th>
                <th>Why it's needed</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>activeTab</code></td>
                <td>Capture the tab you're on, only when you click the extension or use its shortcut or menu</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>scripting</code></td>
                <td>Show the area-selection overlay and scroll the page to build full-page captures</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>tabCapture</code></td>
                <td>Record the current tab</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>offscreen</code></td>
                <td>Run the tab recorder in the background while you keep using the page</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>downloads</code></td>
                <td>Save screenshots and recordings to your Downloads folder</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>storage</code>, <code>unlimitedStorage</code></td>
                <td>Keep your settings and local capture history (images and videos can be large)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>contextMenus</code></td>
                <td>Right-click menu shortcuts for capturing</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>clipboardWrite</code></td>
                <td>Copy screenshots to your clipboard</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>The extension is not directed at children and collects no information from anyone.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be published at the same address with a new "Last updated" date.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:rohithk422@gmail.com">rohithk422@gmail.com</a></p>
      </article>
      <footer>Enhanced Screen Capture</footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
